Good — I can help you prepare. Below I’ve grouped the most useful things to check, the specific questions to ask Dr. Chen, which tests might be appropriate, and what would make a gastroenterology referral reasonable. If you’d like, I can also draft a short message or email to Dr. Chen summarizing these points.

Key context/clarifying questions (quick)
- Are you female or male? (Bone risk interpretation differs for premenopausal women vs men.)
- Have you ever had a DEXA (bone density) scan? If yes, when and what were the results (T-score/Z-score)?
