- “I’ve taken prednisone tapers — do I need testing or prophylaxis for GI issues, or only if I have symptoms?”

Other practical items:
- “Can you review my current levothyroxine dose and last TSH to make sure I’m not over‑replaced?”
- “Given my stroke history, should we review fall-risk reduction or consider physical therapy/balance training?”

E. Immediate next steps I recommend
- If you don’t know your DXA status: ask Dr. Chen whether one exists and request a copy. If none, discuss whether to get DXA now.
- Get baseline labs: 25‑OH vitamin D, TSH, CMP (calcium, creatinine).
- Note and document your prednisone exposure (dates, dose, how often) so your PCP can assess steroid-related risk.
- Check whether you’re on antiplatelet/anticoagulant therapy and whether you have GI symptoms or family history of colon cancer.

